            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Works and Styles</strong><br>\nThroughout his life, Picasso experimented with different techniques, styles, and materials. His later works were a mix of various styles from his past, with vibrant colors, bold shapes, and a renewed interest in painting and sculpture.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Character</strong><br>\nPicasso's personal life was as tumultuous and vibrant as his art, including numerous love affairs and marriages. His personality was as large as his legacy, with a charisma and fervor for life that was evident in his prolific output.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Enduring Legacy</strong><br>\nPicasso passed away in 1973 at the age of 91, leaving behind an immense body of work, including over 20,000 paintings, drawings, sculptures, ceramics, and prints. His innovative contributions to modern art continue to influence and challenge artists today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
